# Ancient Cornucopia: "gain 1 life for each of that spell's colors" and the ruling: "Ancient Cornucopia's triggered ability resolves
# before the spell that caused it to trigger. The ability will resolve even if that spell is countered. If that spell is
# countered, use its last known information to determine what colors it was." On turn 3 Bot1 casts Lightning Helix (red and white);
# with Cornucopia's trigger on top of it, Bot2 counters the Helix with Counterspell (itself a blue spell, which does not trigger
# Bot1's Cornucopia: "you cast"). The Helix is countered before the trigger resolves; Bot1 still accepts and gains 2 life (the Helix's
# two colors), and takes no gain from the Helix itself (3 damage and 3 life never happen).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Ancient Cornucopia
Lightning Helix
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancient Cornucopia.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Helix.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Lightning Helix)
! Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Helix
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
